<% content_for :title, @category.name %>

<%= page_header(
    title: @category.name,
    subtitle: "#{@category.category_type.titleize} category details and management",
    breadcrumbs: [
      { label: "Categories", url: categories_path(type: @category.category_type) },
      { label: @category.name }
    ],
    actions: [
      {
        label: "Manage Items",
        url: category_items_path(@category),
        class: "inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 rounded border border-gray-300 bg-white text-gray-700 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-gray-50 shadow-sm transition"
      },
      {
        label: "Edit",
        url: edit_category_path(@category),
        class: "inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 rounded border border-gray-300 bg-white text-gray-700 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-gray-50 shadow-sm transition"
      },
      {
        label: "Delete",
        url: category_path(@category),
        method: :delete,
        class: "inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 rounded bg-status-danger text-white text-sm font-medium hover:opacity-90 shadow-sm transition",
        confirm: "Are you sure you want to delete #{@category.name}? This will permanently delete all #{@category.items.size} item(s) and #{@category.entries.size} entry/entries. This action cannot be undone."
      }
    ]
) %>

<div class="container mx-auto px-4 py-6">
  <%= render "categories/_partials/show/category_banner", category: @category %>

  <%= render "shared/period_toggle",
      monthly_path: category_path(@category),
      ytd_path: category_path(@category, period: "ytd") %>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
    <%# THE CACHE COVERS THE LEFT COLUMN ONLY, and the holdings card is why.

        It used to wrap both columns. Every figure inside it is derived from THIS category's own
        entries, and `Entry belongs_to :item, touch: true` / `Item belongs_to :category, touch: true`
        move `@category.updated_at` whenever one of those changes — so the key is sound for exactly
        the figures it holds.

        WHAT A CATEGORY HOLDS IS NOT ONE OF THEM. Its balance moves when a distribution writes an
        `Allocation`, or when money is moved in or out by hand, and neither of those touches the
        category through an entry: the card would go on printing last week's `$240.00 left` under a
        live "Rules on the Budget page" link. It is outside the cache, and the left column — the
        spending figures the period toggle is for — keeps it.

        `@category.pool` IS OUT OF THE KEY (Task 7). It was there because `_summary_card` printed
        the pool's noun and name, so a renamed pool had to bust this fragment; the summary card
        names no pool now — nothing in this app does, for a category — and `belongs_to :pool` is a
        dying lane the whole page has stopped reading. Keying on a column no rendered byte depends
        on buys nothing and outlives the association.

        Cheap: the right column costs two COUNTs and the five preloaded recent entries. %>
    <!-- Left Column -->
    <div class="lg:col-span-2 space-y-6">
      <%# `pace_cache_key(selected_date)` left this key with the daily ramp it existed for: a
          prorated cap's "expected by today" figure changed every day, so the key had to as well.
          Proration is deleted (plan 3, task 3) and nothing under this cache moves with the clock. %>
      <% cache [@category, selected_date, current_period] do %>
        <%= render "categories/_partials/show/summary_card", category: @category %>
        <%= render "categories/_partials/show/items_list", category: @category %>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <!-- Right Column -->
    <div class="space-y-6">
      <%= render "categories/_partials/show/details_card", category: @category %>

      <%# EVERY EXPENSE CATEGORY, in the two states one can be in — holding its own money, or
          spending what's available. An income category holds nothing and gets no card. %>
      <% if @holdings_card %>
        <%= render "categories/_partials/show/holdings_card", presenter: @holdings_card %>
      <% end %>

      <%= render "categories/_partials/show/recent_activity", category: @category %>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
